				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">04</span>
					<h3>Drafting Affidavits</h3>
					<p>We draft affidavits that clearly explain executor authority, explain the will’s validity, and provide essential estate information, 
                    ensuring the Supreme Court receives complete details during the probate application process and minimising the risk of requisitions that can slow the progress of an application.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Vacant Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">05</span>
					<h3>Requisition Responses</h3>
					<p>If requisitions arise, we respond promptly and accurately, addressing the Court’s concerns and supplying any additional information needed to continue processing the probate application, 
                    ensuring the estate remains compliant with probate requirements NSW imposes throughout the process.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Rural Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">06</span>
					<h3>Estate Administration</h3>
					<p>After the Grant of Probate is issued, we are able to support executors through the estate administration process, including collecting assets, paying debts, effecting property sales and/or transfers 
                    (subject always to the terms of the will), paying tax liabilities, defending claims against the estate, and guiding them through each step, ensuring the estate is finalised smoothly and in compliance with NSW estate administration rules.</p>
